Ignis: let an embedder plug a reactor into the reference scheduler's idle point.

Where ext/test_scheduler raises DeadlockError ("this scheduler has no reactor
to deliver it"), call a process-wide hook first; if the hook enqueued
something, continue the loop. Applied on top of true-async/php-src async-core
commit 14af3cb by scripts/build-php-async.sh. ~15 lines, no behaviour change
when no hook is set.
--- a/ext/test_scheduler/test_scheduler.c
+++ b/ext/test_scheduler/test_scheduler.c
@@ -178,6 +178,16 @@
 static zend_class_entry *ts_ce_deadlock_error;
 static zend_object_handlers ts_coroutine_handlers;
 
+/* Ignis idle hook: called when the run queue is empty but coroutines are
+ * still parked. Returns true if it enqueued at least one coroutine. */
+typedef bool (*ts_idle_hook_t)(void);
+static ts_idle_hook_t ts_idle_hook = NULL;
+ZEND_API void test_scheduler_set_idle_hook(ts_idle_hook_t hook);
+ZEND_API void test_scheduler_set_idle_hook(ts_idle_hook_t hook)
+{
+	ts_idle_hook = hook;
+}
+
 /* The bottom frame of every coroutine's VM stack. Nameless on purpose: a
  * frame with no function name is a dummy frame, and backtraces skip it — the
  * engine's own fiber root frame is built exactly this way. */
@@ -1143,6 +1153,11 @@
 				if (zend_hash_num_elements(&TSG(coroutines)) == 0) {
 					break;
 				}
+				/* Ignis: a real reactor may deliver a wakeup here. */
+				if (ts_idle_hook != NULL && ts_idle_hook()) {
+					continue;
+				}
+
 				/* Nothing runnable, yet coroutines are still alive: they
 				 * wait for something that will never happen, because this
 				 * scheduler has no reactor to deliver it. */
